{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD_eq_qsq_div_bracketTwo_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD_eq_qsq_div_bracketTwo_real","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L223-L228","doc":"**`z_D(q) = q²/[2]_q`** — the archimedean specialisation of\n`zD_eq_qsq_div_bracketTwo`, matching the definition `zD`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD_eq_qsq_div_bracketTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD_eq_qsq_div_bracketTwo","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L218-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff_sign_separates_zC_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff_sign_separates_zC_zD","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L185-L199","doc":"**The two conventions sit on opposite sides of `z = 1/2`.**\n\nCapstone: for every substrate value `q > 1` the ladder's affine phase\ncoefficient is positive at `z_C` and negative at `z_D`.  There is no\n`q > 1` at which the two agree in sign, so the C ladder's phase formula\ncannot be transported to D by substituting the parameter.\n\n**This is a statement about one ansatz's phase, not about either\ntrace.**  The earlier reading — that it separates the conventions by\n*positivity of a Wedderburn weight* — is retracted (module docstring):\nunder convention D the `H₃(q)` weights are positive semidefinite,\nsignature `(5, 0, 1)`, per S2 (PR #5185). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff_pos_at_zC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff_pos_at_zC","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L176-L183","doc":"**The ladder's affine phase coefficient is strictly positive at `z_C`,\nfor every `q > 1`** — the mirror of `ladderPhaseCoeff_neg_at_zD`, and\nlikewise carrying no trace-positivity content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zC_lt_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zC_lt_half","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L162-L174","doc":"**`z_C(q) < 1/2` on the whole substrate regime `q > 1`.**\n\nWith `s = √q > 1`, the claim `2s < 1 + s²` is `0 < (s − 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff_neg_at_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff_neg_at_zD","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L144-L160","doc":"**The ladder's affine phase coefficient is strictly negative at `z_D`,\nfor every `q > 1`.**\n\nImmediate from `zD_gt_half`.  Its content is exactly that `z_D` lies\nabove `1/2` throughout the substrate regime, so the ladder ansatz's\nphase `α = (z_D − 1)h/2` sits on the far side of `−h/4` from where\nconvention C puts it.\n\n**No trace-positivity content.**  `1/2 − z` is not a Wedderburn weight\n(module docstring); the actual convention-D weight `y_(2,1) = q²/(q²+1)²`\nis strictly *positive*.  Do not read this as \"convention D has a negative\nweight\" — that reading is retracted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD_gt_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD_gt_half","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L133-L142","doc":"**`z_D(q) > 1/2` on the whole substrate regime `q > 1`.**\n\nThe cubic `2q³ − q² − 1` factors as `(q − 1)(2q² + q + 1)`, whose second\nfactor is positive for all real `q`; so the inequality is strict and\nholds for every `q > 1`, degenerating to equality only at the classical\npoint `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.ladderPhaseCoeff","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L117-L131","doc":"The Q_β ladder's **affine phase coefficient**, `1/2 − z`.\n\nThe ladder's phase satisfies `α = (z−1)h/2 = −h/4 − (h/2)·(1/2 − z)`,\npure algebra, so this is the single quantity through which the Markov\nparameter `z` reaches the ladder.\n\n**This is not a Wedderburn weight.**  It was previously named\n`threeRowMiddleWeight` and identified with the standard-block weight\n`y_(2,1)` of `H₃(q)`; that identification is retracted — see the module\ndocstring.  The vector `(z, 1/2 − z, z)` satisfies only the\nnormalisation condition of `CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3` and fails the\nother two, and the actual `y_(2,1)` under convention D is\n`q²/(q²+1)² > 0`.  No positivity claim about any Markov trace follows\nfrom the sign of this coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zC","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L114-L115","doc":"The convention-C Markov parameter, `z_C(q) = √q/(1+q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.zD","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayLadderConventionDPositivity.lean#L111-L112","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter, `z_D(q) = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}